# fimiproxy

## Now

- runtime config changes
- correlated log by req + res (partially: structured accessLog + durationMs)

## Later

- no downtime config changes
- prefer https over http when there's both origin servers
- return artifacts from start calls so callers can perform explicit graceful shutdowns
- add validation checks to config file, and config
- what to do about CONNECT calls
- allow loading JS scripts for dynamic routing
- better code organization
- weighted / sticky load balancing

## Done (performance work)

- multi-process via node:cluster (`workers` config)
- FimiproxyInstance encapsulation (per-process instance state)
- stream.pipeline backpressure on HTTP proxy path
- keep-alive outbound agents
- inbound/outbound timeouts
- async structured JSON logging (`logLevel`, `accessLog`)
- WS open timeout + send backpressure + mutual close
- maxConnections, origin health checks, basic metrics (/metrics + periodic log)
- benchmarks harness (`npm run bench`)
- destroy-on-error / avoid double writeHead
